Implementation detail for preorder enumeration:
```python
def all_preorders(n):
    elems=range(n); pairs=[(i,j) for i in elems for j in elems]
    for mask in range(1<<len(pairs)):
        R={(i,j) for k,(i,j) in enumerate(pairs) if mask>>k & 1}
        if all((i,i) in R for i in elems) and transitive(R): yield R
```
n=4: 65536 iterations, transitive check O(64) → fine.

Chains: all tuples of length 1..n over elems where all pairs i<j satisfy (γ_i,γ_j) ∈ R. With repetition: sequences = sum(n^k) = 340; per preorder 355*340*4 ≈ 480k membership checks — fine.

